# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-safe-recoveries.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/390-read-only-owner-bound-implementation-scope-probe/requirements.md

Feature: Read-only owner-bound implementation scope probe
  Implementation workers need exact mutation authority without changing controller
  or recovery state and without treating Approved spec inputs as writable files.

  @AC1 @SCN001
  Scenario: Probe binds the actual checkout to one current owner
    Given an Approved singular spec and an active implement run
    And exactly one incomplete recovery owner matches the issue, step, root, actual branch, and controller run id
    When the owner-bound publication scope probe runs
    Then the probe succeeds with that owner
    And it derives the branch from Git without a branch or recovery override

  @AC2 @SCN002
  Scenario: Probe is byte-for-byte read-only
    Given run, handoff, recovery, spec, product, and pi-glla state with recorded hashes
    When a successful or rejected probe runs
    Then no controller lock is acquired
    And no recovery record is created or consumed
    And every observed file hash and byte sequence is unchanged

  @AC3 @SCN003
  Scenario: Scope separates writable evidence and read-only inputs
    Given tasks with tracked writes, explicit Download or Generate untracked evidence, Read-only inputs, and Acquire inputs
    When implementation scope is inspected
    Then scope has exactly trackedWritablePaths, untrackedEvidencePaths, taskOperations, readOnlyPaths, and allowedPaths
    And allowedPaths is exactly the writable union
    And spec and exclusively read-only inputs are absent from writable authority

  @AC4 @SCN004
  Scenario: Exact PathCast issue 108 scope excludes its spec
    Given the exact canonical PathCast T001 through T004 fixture
    And run branch main disagrees with the actual and owner branch 108-establish-claim-specific-ip-and-product-safety-guardrails
    When the probe runs with the matching PathCast controller run id
    Then it reports the branch discrepancy
    And it reports 12 tracked writable paths
    And it reports six explicitly untracked evidence paths
    And it reports exactly 18 allowed paths
    And no PathCast spec file is writable or allowed

  @AC5 @SCN005
  Scenario: Task-relative operations reduce deterministically
    Given a path is read-only in one task and writable in another
    And duplicate path operations include Create followed by Modify
    When task scope is reduced
    Then all task and source provenance remains visible
    And the aggregate path is tracked writable and allowed, not read-only

  @AC5 @SCN006
  Scenario Outline: Invalid declarations fail closed
    Given an Approved task with a <defect> declaration
    When implementation scope is inspected
    Then publication_scope_unproven identifies the task and declaration location

    Examples:
      | defect |
      | missing canonical File(s) |
      | near-miss Files label |
      | duplicate canonical File(s) |
      | ambiguous operation |
      | unsupported operation |

  @AC6 @SCN007
  Scenario: Every publication consumer uses structured allowed paths
    Given structured implementation scope excludes all spec files
    When execute, write-code, apply-review, delivery, bind, or reconcile consumes scope
    Then mutation authorization comes only from scope allowedPaths
    And no consumer reconstructs or widens the allowlist

  @AC6 @SCN009
  Scenario: Supervisor bind fixture uses canonical dirty authority
    Given the valid-subject supervisor fixture declares File(s) src/code.mjs with Modify authority
    And src/code.mjs is dirty
    When the supervisor binds the valid subject
    Then publication scope is proven and the bind succeeds
    And subjectless and wrong-issue bind assertions still fail closed

  @AC7 @SCN010
  Scenario: CI remediation preserves worker and evidence boundaries
    Given extension-command and rendered-prompt expectations are satisfied through the authorized write-code workflow
    And the verification report is declared delivery-owner only
    When implementation scope is inspected
    Then neither those test paths nor the verification report enters allowedPaths

  @AC7 @SCN008
  Scenario: Public workflow distinguishes probe from publication mutation
    Given the installed documentation and write-code workflow
    When an implementation worker prepares to edit
    Then it runs the owner-bound read-only probe with issue, implement step, exact spec, and controller run id
    And it reads only scope allowedPaths for edits
    And subject bind remains a later state-changing publication boundary
